      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "You are helping a beginner student learning arrays in JavaScript.\n\nAdd 3 to 5 new items to the existing array. Keep all original items unchanged. Do not rename the array.\n\nUpdate the array by editing the list inside the brackets. Do not use methods like .push() or create new variables.\n\nReturn only the full updated array as valid JavaScript. No explanation, no extra text.\n\nExample:\n\nBefore:\nlet favoritesArray = [\"pizza\", \"tacos\", \"pasta\"];\n\nAfter:\nlet favoritesArray = [\"pizza\", \"tacos\", \"pasta\", \"burger\", \"ramen\", \"sushi\"];"
